% You should not change anything in this file unless you really know
% what you are doing.
%
% DEVIATIONS FROM THE DEPARTMENTAL TEMPLATE (thesis_templates/Thesis Template
% PG/buetcsepgthesis.sty). Confirm these with the department before submission.
% Diffed line by line against the template; the list below is complete.
%
% Three deviations are kept, each for a reason that was measured rather than
% assumed. Removing each one was tried, built, and inspected; the cost recorded
% below is what that build showed.
%
% KEPT, a BUG FIX to an inherited defect rather than a style choice:
%   \RequirePackage{setspace} moves from after hyperref to before it. Both
%   redefine \@footnotetext and the later load discards the earlier one, so in
%   the template's order hyperref's footnote anchors are never written. Measured
%   both ways on this document: in the template's order this document's two
%   footnote destinations both resolve to the cover page, and in this order they
%   resolve to printed pages 44 and 70, where the footnotes are -- PDF sheets 61
%   and 87, the seventeen pages of front matter being the offset. Neither build
%   reports an error or a warning, which is why the defect survives in the
%   template -- and a build with no footnotes would not show it at all.
%   \onehalfspacing still fires at its original position below, so only the load
%   order moves; the spacing and the pagination are unchanged.
%
% KEPT, because the template's own \headheight cannot hold the alternative:
%   \fancyhead[L] wraps \rightmark in \nouppercase, so running heads are set in
%   mixed case rather than upcased. Removing it was tried and reverted. Upcased
%   heads are wider, and two section titles then wrap to two lines -- Sec 6.8
%   and Sec 9.7, on pages 64, 65, 66 and 117. A two-line head needs 27.03pt of
%   \headheight against the 15.0pt set below, so fancyhdr warns four times and
%   the head grows upward into the top margin, sitting about a line and a half
%   higher on those four pages than on every other page. Raising \headheight
%   would trade this deviation for a second one in the page geometry. Pagination
%   is identical either way, so this is the cheaper of the two.
%
% KEPT, and the one remaining change to how the document renders:
%   \section, \subsection and \subsubsection are redefined -- new lines in this
%   file, but they override report.cls. The definitions are report.cls's own
%   with \raggedright appended, so long headings break on words rather than
%   being justified to the margin. No heading text, spacing or numbering
%   differs. Removing them was tried and reverted: it costs three underfull
%   hboxes, at badness 2173, 2080 and 3724, on the Sec 1.2, 1.5.1 and 9.8
%   titles, which is a visibly stretched first line on each of the three.
%
% Everything else is additive: five package loads the template does not carry --
% helvet, array, multicol, tikz and pgfplots -- the three-colour figure palette
% defined beside them, together with the L{} column type
% that array provides, the verbatimblock listing style, the agrplot axis style,
% the Helvetica 92% scaling that matches the sans face optically to Times, and
% one microtype option, nopatch=footnote, documented where it is set. microtype,
% listings, cleveref and imakeidx are the template's own loads, carried forward
% unchanged rather than added here.
%
\RequirePackage[nofancy,notoday]{rcsinfo}
\rcsInfo $Id: buetcsepgthesis.sty,v 1.03 2019/09/29 15:44:58 masroor Exp $

\RequirePackage{graphicx}
